#====================================================================
# DRAFT-sfront-0.99-nested-make-pregenerated-parser-and-cpp-gcc
# sfront on HarmonyOS: nested-make build entry, pre-generated bison
# parser determinism, and the -cpp mode that hard-codes gcc
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-sfront-0.99-nested-make-pregenerated-parser-and-cpp-gcc
trigger_tool:           clang|make|bison|qemu-aarch64|conan|python3
phase:                  source|build|testing
error_signature:        make.*jobserver unavailable|optimization flag '-fno-schedule-insns'
                        is not supported|cannot open rcrt1.o|Pre-processing for file .* was not
                        successful|Cannot open -orc file|Misformed token or string on SASL line

severity:               2
category:               raw-makefile|nested-make|codegen|pregenerated-parser|cli-tool|consumer-test|OHOS
match_keywords:         sfront, SAOL, MP4-SA, libmaker, nested make, MAKEFLAGS, jobserver,
                        parser.tab.c, bison, pre-generated parser, touch, -m32, -fno-schedule-insns,
                        -ansi, __STRICT_ANSI__, -cpp, cppsystemcall, SAOLLIBDIR, /usr/share/sfront,
                        system(NULL), -static, -static-pie, rcrt1.o, qemu-aarch64, EM_AARCH64,
                        bitstream round-trip, symbol renaming, float literal formatting,
                        R38, commands.json, test_package, HarmonyOS, aarch64, musl
title:                  sfront 0.99 on HarmonyOS needs the nested src/lib make entry, a deterministic pre-generated parser, and -cpp ruled out

root_cause:             >
                        sfront 0.99 is 2011-era C89 with two hand-written Makefiles and no
                        configure. src/Makefile hard-codes CC=gcc, MODEL=-m32,
                        ECHECK="-ansi -Wall" and SLOWSCHED=-fno-schedule-insns, so a
                        cross build has to override CFLAGS wholesale (the -m32 ABI does not
                        exist on AArch64) and clear SLOWSCHED (a GCC-only switch clang
                        merely warns about). The real build entry point is src/lib/Makefile,
                        not src/Makefile: its all target builds the libmaker code generator,
                        regenerates the five *lib.[ch] runtime sources from
                        src/lib/{csrc,asys,csys,nsys,psys} templates and only then descends
                        into src/Makefile, so command-line variable overrides have to travel
                        through MAKEFLAGS and the sub-make cannot inherit a jobserver over
                        HMDFS. src/Makefile also carries a parser.tab.c rule whose recipe is
                        "-bison -d parser.y" with a leading '-' that makes make ignore the
                        failure: the official tarball already ships the bison 2.3 output, but
                        conan get() does not preserve mtimes, so whether make treats the
                        shipped parser as stale depends on extraction order and on whether
                        bison happens to exist - the build silently becomes non-deterministic.
                        Finally the -cpp mode is unavailable on OHOS: sfmain.c:cppsystemcall
                        hard-codes the external program "gcc -nostdinc -x c++ -E" and appends
                        the compile-time constant SAOLLIBDIR (tree.h:667) = "/usr/share/sfront".

affected_scope:         >
                        Historical C projects whose real build lives in a nested Makefile that
                        re-enters the top-level one, that ship pre-generated parser/lexer
                        output next to the grammar, and whose optional preprocessing mode
                        names an external tool by absolute/literal name. Directly applicable to
                        raw-Makefile OHOS CLI adaptations; the -static vs -static-pie and
                        nested-make findings generalise to any OHOS CLI package.

verification_cmd:       >
                        conan create archives/s/sfront/0.99 --name=sfront --version=0.99
                        -pr:h=ohos-aarch64-wsl -pr:b=ohos-aarch64-wsl --build=missing
        (expect rc=0 and "SFRONT_TEST_SUMMARY pass=68 fail=0 total=68");
        CI_PACKAGES="archives/s/sfront/0.99" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh;
        after packaging, `od -An -tx1 -j18 -N2 <package>/bin/sfront` must print b700 (EM_AARCH64).

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           nested-make-entry-touch-pregenerated-parser-static-delivery
rec_description:        >
                        Build through src/lib/Makefile with -j1, overriding
                        CFLAGS="-O2 -Wall -Werror=implicit-function-declaration -static" and
                        SLOWSCHED=, reading the compiler from
                        tools.build:compiler_executables. Touch the shipped parser.tab.c /
                        parser.tab.h so the pre-generated bison output is authoritative and the
                        build no longer depends on bison being installed. Deliver a -static
                        executable so it runs both natively on an AArch64 worker and under
                        qemu-aarch64 on x86 without a guest rootfs. Declare -cpp as
                        unavailable on OHOS with the sfmain.c/tree.h evidence instead of
                        dropping the one example that needs it.

rec_command:            >
        touch parser.tab.c parser.tab.h;
        make -C src/lib -j1 "CC=$cc" SLOWSCHED= LINKLIB=-lm \
          CFLAGS="-O2 -Wall -Werror=implicit-function-declaration -static";
        # -static-pie is unavailable on OHOS: ld.lld-15: error: cannot open rcrt1.o

rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               sfront-conan-recipe-nested-make

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      bison-tool-requires-instead-of-touch
fallback_description:   >
                        If a project genuinely needs a regenerated parser (its shipped
        parser output is stale, not merely mis-dated), declare
        tool_requires = "bison/3.8.2" and run "make parser.tab.c" explicitly instead of
        touching. Cross-check first that the regenerated parser accepts the grammar without
        errors and produces equivalent translator output.
fallback_command:       >
        conan create archives/<pkg>/<ver> --build=missing -pr:h=ohos-aarch64-wsl \
          -pr:b=ohos-aarch64-wsl   with tool_requires = "bison/3.8.2"
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          bison-tool-requires

forbid_1_pattern:       make\s+-C\s+src\s|make\s+src/Makefile|cd src\s*&&\s*make\s+sfront
forbid_1_reason:        >
                        Building src/Makefile directly skips libmaker, so the five
                        *lib.[ch] runtime sources the translator embeds into every generated
                        program are never regenerated from src/lib/*/ templates.
forbid_1_consequence:   >
                        The translator links against whatever stale copies the tarball
                        happens to carry, or fails to link on a clean tree.

forbid_2_pattern:       touch\s+parser\.tab\.[ch].*\n.*bison|apt.*bison.*install.*without.*tool_requires
forbid_2_reason:        >
                        Either regenerating with an undeclared bison, or trusting extraction
                        order to decide whether the shipped parser is current, makes the
                        build result depend on the machine.
forbid_2_consequence:   >
                        The same recipe produces different binaries on a developer box and on
                        a CI worker, and CI fails with "bison: command not found" only on the
                machines that lack it.

forbid_3_pattern:       -cpp|SAOLLIBDIR
forbid_3_reason:        >
                        sfront's -cpp path shells out to a literal "gcc" and to the absolute
                        path /usr/share/sfront; neither exists in the OHOS toolchain, and
                pretending otherwise yields "Pre-processing for file X was not successful".
forbid_3_consequence:   >
                        Any test or recipe that depends on -cpp fails at runtime on OHOS while
        looking correct on a desktop Linux box with gcc installed.

forbid_4_pattern:       -static-pie|rcrt1\.o
forbid_4_reason:        >
                        The OHOS NDK ships no static-pie startup files, so -static-pie fails to
        link with "cannot open rcrt1.o".
forbid_4_consequence:   >
                        The link step fails late, after the whole tree has been compiled.

forbid_5_pattern:       cmp.*orc\.c.*frombit\.c|diff.*orc\.c.*frombit\.c
forbid_5_reason:        >
                        A bitstream round-trip renames SAOL identifiers to generated names
                        (a7_*) and re-formats float literals (1.95F -> 1.950000e+00F); the
                two programs are semantically equal but never textually equal, and -symtab
                        does not preserve the names.
forbid_5_consequence:   >
                        A correct translator looks broken, and the real equivalence (the
        rendered audio) is never checked.

